I've gone through the new finfo interface, there are some questions regarding how it can be used for kfd ioctl decoding

In `ioctl_decode`, `finfo` is NULL when it is leaving or the fd is not valid
  * kfd and kd still needs distinguishing when in leaving stages
  * in tests we are always using fd = -1

The leaving stage problem can be resolved by changing the logic in `SYS_FUNC(ioctl)`, but for the tests there are no way to provide finfo.

In summary, there must be some fallback ways to distinguish kfd and kd, and the code looks like this

```
if (finfo) {
  // call kfd_ioctl or kd_ioctl accoring to the finfo
} else {
  if (_IOC_NR(code) >= _IOC_NR(KIOCSOUND))
  // ...
}
```

And the current ugly hack can not be avoided.

Since we always need a fallback way, and there is actualy no overlap for now, I think kfd/kd distinguish can just use the hacky way for now to reduce the complexity. In the future when there are overlaps, finfo could be used.

